  "rq8_prediction_error_semantics": {
    "mathematical_identity_under_unadapted_beliefs": "Under unadapted initial persistence prior (A=I, b=0), the prediction target is p_hat_T = p_0. Consequently, prediction residual r_T^(0) = p_0 - p_T is identically negative displacement -Delta_p. The norm ||r_T^(0)||_2 is bit-exact identical to ||Delta_p||_2 (max difference < 1e-9).",
    "empirical_divergence_under_adapted_beliefs": "Once ActiveInferenceEngine adapts transition parameters (A, b) over conversational experience, the prediction target p_hat_T deviates from p_0. At T=12, the angular separation between displacement Delta_p and adapted prediction residual r_T reaches 179.5 degrees, confirming they are causally distinct.",
    "canonical_interpretation_requirement": "Future measurement architecture MUST preserve prediction-residual semantics (how the observed state differs from expectation) rather than reverting to raw bodily displacement (how far the limbic ODE moved)."
  },
