  "final_synthesis": {
    "final_state": "State B \u2014 Minimal Side-Channel Appears Sufficient to Avoid Collapse",
    "rationale": "Empirical ablation evidence across T <= 25 demonstrates that canonical scalar S loses directional/component information, resulting in 358 cross-tier collapse pairs at T=12. However, full 3D vector replacement (R5) is NOT minimal because Dominance can be ablated (A3) without degrading collapse resolution. A minimal side-channel retaining discrete sign polarity [S, sign(r)] (R3) or normalized direction [S, r/||r||] (R2) completely eliminates cross-tier collapse (0 collapses) while preserving canonical scalar surprise as the primary intensity metric. Therefore, a minimal side-channel appears sufficient to avoid directional collapse under the evaluated conditions. However, this finding is strictly an empirical property of the frozen G1 evaluation set; promoting any side-channel to production remains strictly unauthorized.",
